sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: To inscribe in a given circle a triangle equiangular with a given triangle.
----
proof:

Let {ABC} be the given circle, and {DEF} the given triangle.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="350" height="290" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IV.2 diagram" src="propIV2.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // The tangent at A, the two I.23 angle copies at A, the join BC, then
    // the III.32 alternate-segment argument twice and I.32 for the third
    // angle.
    //
    // Joyce's figure builds the circle from the triangle: A and B are free,
    // C is the `similar` point making ABC similar to DEF, and the circle is
    // the circumcircle of ABC. The walk follows the proof's order instead
    // — circle and triangle given, A on the circle, the angles at A copied
    // — which the figure supports unchanged.
    //
    // Everything added leaves the resting figure as it was. AH and AG (the
    // two halves of the tangent the proof names) and the arc arcB are
    // transparent highlight targets. AC and BC are solid black lines over
    // the sides of triABC, hidden at rest (initiallyHidden): the slides
    // need the sides one at a time, in the order the construction draws
    // them, and triABC's blue face arrives only on the closing slide. AB is
    // Joyce's own line.
    //
    // Angle markers: equal angles share a colour — DEF, HAC and ABC blue;
    // DFE, GAB and ACB green; EDF and BAC purple. The three markers at A
    // lie side by side along the tangent rather than nested, so all three
    // are pinned at 22 px to opt out of same-vertex ring stepping. No angle
    // is called right in this proof, so there is no right-angle mark.
    var GIVEN = ["circABC","DEF","D","E","F"];
    var TANG  = GIVEN.concat(["A","G","H","GH","AH","AG"]);
    var ANG1  = TANG.concat(["angE","AC","C","angHAC"]);
    var ANG2  = ANG1.concat(["angF","AB","B","angGAB"]);
    var JOIN  = ANG2.concat(["BC"]);
    var ALT1  = JOIN.concat(["angB","arcB"]);
    var ALT2  = ALT1.concat(["angC"]);
    var REM   = ALT2.concat(["angA","angD"]);
    var DONE  = REM.concat(["triABC"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IV.2",
        elements: [
            "D;point;free;250,180",
            "E;point;free;230,50",
            "F;point;free;320,130",
            "DEF;polygon;triangle;D,E,F;0;0;black;random",
            "A;point;free;100,220",
            "B;point;free;110,40",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "C;point;similar;A,B,D,E,F",
            "circABC;circle;circumcircle;A,B,C;0;0;black;random",
            "triABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;black;random",
            "O;point;center;circABC;0;0",
            "AG';line;perpendicular;A,O;0;0;0",
            "G;point;lineSlider;AG',35,190",
            "H;point;lineSlider;AG',200,250",
            "GH;line;connect;G,H",
            // The two parts of the tangent the proof names.
            "AH;line;connect;A,H;0;0;0",
            "AG;line;connect;A,G;0;0;0",
            // The sides AC and BC, drawn A to C and B to C as the
            // construction joins them; hidden at rest (see above).
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            // The circumference of the alternate segment: from A through B
            // to C, on the side of AC away from H.
            "arcB;sector;arc;C,B,A;0;0;0;0",
            "angE;sector;angleMarker;E,D,F;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angF;sector;angleMarker;F,D,E;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angD;sector;angleMarker;D,E,F;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angHAC;sector;angleMarker;A,H,C,22;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angGAB;sector;angleMarker;A,G,B,22;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angA;sector;angleMarker;A,B,C,22;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angB;sector;angleMarker;B,A,C;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angC;sector;angleMarker;C,A,B;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0"
        ],
        // Draggables (checked against the bundle): D, E, F, A, B free; G, H
        // lineSliders on the tangent. D, E, F are the given triangle and
        // stand from slide 1. A is not taken until "touching the circle at
        // A", G and H arrive with the tangent, and B with the angle GAB, so
        // those four are deferred and follow `visible`. C (similar) is
        // derived and listed per slide. The resting figure is unaffected.
        deferDraggables: ["A","B","G","H"],
        initiallyHidden: ["AC","BC"],
        // The circle owns the name ABC in prose; the angle ABC takes the
        // display override {ABC|angB}, and the angle DEF {DEF|angE}, since
        // the triangle owns DEF.
        aliases: { "ABC": "circABC", "HG": "GH", "HA": "AH", "GA": "AG",
                   "CA": "AC", "BA": "AB", "CB": "BC",
                   "HAC": "angHAC", "CAH": "angHAC",
                   "GAB": "angGAB", "BAG": "angGAB",
                   "DFE": "angF", "EFD": "angF",
                   "EDF": "angD", "FDE": "angD",
                   "BAC": "angA", "CAB": "angA",
                   "ACB": "angC", "BCA": "angC" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“To inscribe in a given circle a triangle equiangular with a given triangle.”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["circABC","DEF"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "IV.2" }] },
            { text: "Let {ABC} be the given circle, and {DEF} the given triangle.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["circABC","DEF"] },
            { text: "It is required to inscribe a triangle equiangular with the triangle {DEF} in the circle {ABC}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["DEF","circABC"] },
            { text: "Draw {GH} touching the circle {ABC} at {A}.",
              visible: TANG,
              highlighted: ["GH","A"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "A",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "GH", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "GH touches the circle at A", ref: "III.16,Cor" }] },
            { text: "Construct the angle {HAC} equal to the angle {DEF|angE} on the straight line {AH} and at the point {A} on it,",
              visible: ANG1,
              highlighted: ["AH","A"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angE",   name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "AC",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "C",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "angHAC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle HAC = angle DEF", ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "and construct the angle {GAB} equal to the angle {DFE} on the straight line {AG} and at the point {A} on it.",
              visible: ANG2,
              highlighted: ["AG","A"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angF",   name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "AB",     name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "B",      name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "angGAB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle GAB = angle DFE", ref: "I.23" }] },
            { text: "Join {BC}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["BC"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "BC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Then, since a straight line {AH} touches the circle {ABC},",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AH","circABC"] },
            { text: "and from the point of contact at {A} the straight line {AC} is drawn across in the circle,",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["A","AC"] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {HAC} equals the angle {ABC|angB} in {the alternate segment|arcB} of the circle.",
              visible: ALT1,
              highlighted: ["angHAC","angB","arcB","AC"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle HAC = angle ABC in the alternate segment", ref: "III.32" }] },
            { text: "But the angle {HAC} equals the angle {DEF|angE}, therefore the angle {ABC|angB} also equals the angle {DEF|angE}.",
              visible: ALT1,
              highlighted: ["angHAC","angE","angB"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "equal to the same angle HAC", ref: "C.N.1" }] },
            { text: "For the same reason the angle {ACB} also equals the angle {DFE},",
              visible: ALT2,
              highlighted: ["angGAB","angC","angF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [
                  { claim: "angle GAB = angle ACB in the alternate segment", ref: "III.32" },
                  { claim: "angle GAB = angle DFE", ref: "C.N.1" } ] },
            { text: "therefore the remaining angle {BAC} also equals the remaining angle {EDF}.",
              visible: REM,
              highlighted: ["angA","angD"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "the three angles of a triangle equal two right angles", ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "Therefore a triangle equiangular with the given triangle has been inscribed in the given circle.",
              visible: DONE,
              highlighted: ["angA","angB","angC","angD","angE","angF"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "triABC", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] },
              justifications: [
                  { claim: "each angle of ABC touches the circumference", ref: "IV.Def.2" },
                  { ref: "Q.E.F." } ] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "IV.2") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1":   "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "C.N.1":      "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn1/",
        "I.23":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI23/",
        "I.32":       "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI32/",
        "III.16,Cor": "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII16/#cor",
        "III.32":     "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII32/",
        "IV.Def.2":   "/elements/books/bookIV/definitions/defIV2/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

It is required to inscribe a triangle equiangular with the triangle {DEF} in the circle {ABC}.

<div class="just"><a href="/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII16/#cor">III.16,Cor</a></div>

Draw {GH} touching the circle {ABC} at {A}.

Construct the angle {HAC} equal to the angle {DEF|angE} on the straight line {AH} and at the point {A} on it, and construct the angle {GAB} equal to the angle {DFE} on the straight line {AG} and at the point {A} on it. Join {BC}. [!just I.23]

Then, since a straight line {AH} touches the circle {ABC}, and from the point of contact at {A} the straight line {AC} is drawn across in the circle, therefore the angle {HAC} equals the angle {ABC|angB} in the alternate segment of the circle. [!just III.32]

But the angle {HAC} equals the angle {DEF|angE}, therefore the angle {ABC|angB} also equals the angle {DEF|angE}.

For the same reason the angle {ACB} also equals the angle {DFE}, therefore the remaining angle {BAC} also equals the remaining angle {EDF}. [!just I.32]

Therefore a triangle equiangular with the given triangle has been inscribed in the given circle. [!just IV.Def.2]

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
<br clear="all">
----
guide: This construction is used in propositions @IV.11, @IV.16, and @XIII.13.
